    OPT_routeVendorFree = "Plan a vendor at no more than … free slots",
    OPT_routeVendorFree_TIP = "With at most this many free slots in your normal bags, the levelling route plans a vendor (default 4). Only works with \"Plan vendors along the way\".",
    OPT_routeGather = "Pick herbs and ore along the way",
    OPT_routeGather_TIP = "Only with Herbalism or Mining: the levelling route makes short detours to your remembered gathering spots along the way (where you harvested at least twice and your skill is high enough), at most as far as \"Detour limit\". The steps carry the profession's icon, in the menu and on the world map. A remembered spot can be empty right now – then use \"Skip step\".",
    OPT_routeDetour = "Detour limit",
    OPT_routeDetour_TIP = "At most this many yards a vendor or gathering detour of the levelling route may cost (default 60, 0 = only what lies right on the way). If no vendor is that close, the menu only shows a hint.",
    OPT_routeHard = "Plan hard quests",
    OPT_routeHard_TIP = "Elite and dungeon quests as well as quests more than three levels above you are planned like any other. Off – for example when levelling alone – they are listed with a reason under \"Not in the route\".",
    OPT_routeLine = "Levelling route as a line on the world map",
    OPT_routeLine_TIP = "Draws the levelling route as a solid line from gold to orange on Blizzard's world map, from where you are through all steps, with arrows in walking direction; the part to the next step is strong, every further one paler. By default only the next step shows its number with its goal next to it (all numbers with ezMap's switch \"Numbers at every step of the route\"); mouse over the number or the line names the route, step and distance; the start follows you while the map is open, finished steps disappear. Gathering detours show the icon of their profession there. Needs ezMap.",
    OPT_routeMiniArrow = "Levelling route arrow on the minimap",
    OPT_routeMiniArrow_TIP = "What you get: a small golden arrow at the edge of the minimap points to the next step of the levelling route, even when it is far away. When the step is in view, the arrow moves inwards to its place; once you are there, it disappears. It takes no mouse clicks and leaves Blizzard's map pin and arrow alone. Needs ezMap.",
    OPT_routeWatch = "Next quest of the route in Blizzard's tracker",
    OPT_routeWatch_TIP = "Off by default. With this option ezQuest changes Blizzard's quest tracking without a click: the quest of the levelling route's next step is added to the tracker if you do not track it there yet, and removed again as soon as the route moves on or is discarded, likewise after /reload or your next login (for that ezQuest only remembers the quest IDs per character). Only what ezQuest added itself is removed – what you track yourself stays. During combat only afterwards. Questie's own tracker offers no public interface for entries from other addons.",
    OPT_ROUTE_NOW = "Compute the levelling route",
    OPT_ROUTE_NOW_BUTTON = "Compute",
    OPT_ROUTE_NOW_TIP = "Computes the levelling route from your quest log and prints the first steps to the chat. The same is in the gear menu at the top right of the world map's quest list (entry \"Levelling route\"); as a command: /ezquest route. /ezquest status shows the state as well.",
    ROUTE_MENU = "Levelling route",
    ROUTE_MENU_HAS = "Levelling route (%s)",
    ROUTE_MENU_TIP = "An order for the quests in your quest log: bundle objectives in your zone, turn in, no doubling back – lots of experience early. Clicking a step sets Blizzard's map pin (with ezMap; the arrow comes with ezMap's switch \"Turn on navigation\" or by clicking the pin); after a completed objective or a turn-in the pin moves on by itself. Off by default, available as an option below: add the next quest to Blizzard's tracker – without a click. The arrow moves along only with ezMap's switch \"Turn on navigation\".",
    ROUTE_BUILD = "Compute route",
    ROUTE_REBUILD = "Compute again",
    ROUTE_BUILD_TIP = "Computes the route from the quests in your log. Places come from the game and, when Questie runs, according to Questie – only for quests you already have; places and route are not saved (computed again after /reload – by itself with \"Compute the route automatically\").",
    ROUTE_LAST_AUTO = "Computed automatically %s",
    ROUTE_LAST_CLICK = "Computed %s",
    ROUTE_LAST_MS = " (computing time %d ms)",
    ROUTE_LAST_TIP = "When the route was last computed in full. \"Automatically\": without a click – after logging in or once there are quests in your log (option \"Compute the route automatically\") and, even without that option, after abandoning a quest or changing a setting. Since then it only moves on after completed objectives and turn-ins and inserts new quests. The computing time measures the computation itself only.",
    ROUTE_AUTO_WAIT = "No route yet – computed by itself as soon as there are quests in your log",
    ROUTE_AUTO_WAIT_TIP = "With \"Compute the route automatically\" ezQuest computes the route shortly after you log in and, while there is none, as soon as you accept a quest. Only after combat and not while the game does not know where you are (instance, loading screen). \"Compute route\" does it right away.",
    ROUTE_AUTO_NOXP = "Not by itself – you gain no experience right now",
    ROUTE_AUTO_NOXP_TIP = "At maximum level or with experience turned off at a trainer ezQuest does not compute the levelling route by itself; it orders by experience per distance. \"Compute route\" still computes it if you want.",
    ROUTE_AUTO_EMPTY = "No quest of the route near you – computed again after a zone change",
    ROUTE_AUTO_EMPTY_TIP = "The route without a click found no quest with a place near you (another zone, or the places were not ready yet). It is computed again when you change zones, after a loading screen and once shortly after you log in; a new quest is inserted right away.",
    ROUTE_STATUS_NOXP = "Levelling route: not computed yet – you gain no experience right now, so not by itself (if you want: gear at the top right of the quest list, Levelling route, Compute route; the button \"Compute\" on the settings page; or %s).",
    ROUTE_AUTO_HELD = "Automatic computing paused – \"Compute route\" starts it again",
    ROUTE_AUTO_HELD_TIP = "You discarded the route or cancelled its computation; until your next click on \"Compute route\" (or /reload) ezQuest does not compute it again by itself.",
    ROUTE_RUNNING = "Computing … (step %d)",
    ROUTE_RUNNING_TIP = "Many quests: the route is computed over several frames. The result then appears in the chat and here.",
    ROUTE_CANCEL_TIP = "Cancels the running computation. If it ran without a click, ezQuest does not compute again by itself until you click \"Compute route\".",
    ROUTE_STARTED = "Computing the levelling route …",
    ROUTE_SUMMARY = "Levelling route: %s, about %s, about %s XP",
    ROUTE_SUMMARY_NOXP = "Levelling route: %s, about %s, XP unknown",
    ROUTE_SUMMARY_TIP = "Time and experience are estimates: walking about 7 yards per second, about 20 seconds per objective unit; experience according to the quest log, unknown ones with the mean of the known ones – if the quest log gives XP for no quest at all, it says \"XP unknown\" and the order follows distance and time only. Where the places come from:",
    ROUTE_SRC_COUNT = "%s: %d",
